{
  "changes": [
    "Merged the duplicated service-registration alternatives into a single decision with shared register/update handling and kept the mediator supply step separate.",
    "Moved shared/actor-specific steps into the correct lanes: Web Server publishes and initiates; Mediator receives, evaluates, generates, and forwards; Service Registry registers/updates/supplies; Policy Repository returns policies and enforces them; Local Peering Agent handles discovery, negotiation, protocol setup, and lifecycle changes.",
    "Split the peering trigger path so the initialization request is sent only when hotspot/excess load is detected, with timeout and malicious-request exceptions ending the flow.",
    "Added missing mediator retrieval of SR and PR information before generating service requirements, and added the accept/reject decision before passing requirements to the local PA.",
    "Separated long-term policy return from short-term negotiation, then discovery, inter-PA negotiation, and sufficient-resources branching before establishing peering.",
    "Added the operational setup actions for protocol configuration, configuration advertisement, load exchange, request redirection, accounting exchange, and policy deployment.",
    "Consolidated disband/re-arrangement conditions into one lifecycle decision, with an exceptional-circumstances branch that bypasses disbanding and ends the flow."
  ],
  "accepted": true,
  "reason": "no coverage or structural loss",
